From d2461afc8508775d2f82044ca6b1cc771381365d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justin <justurn@live.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 08:24:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: Quest chests stop being interactable once the objective
 is full (I-284)

AC has no quest gate for chest interaction. chest.questId is unused
(GameObjectData.h:92), chests are absent from GameObject::Use, and opening runs
client lock cast -> Spell::EffectOpenLock -> Player::SendLoot without ever
reading quest status. The loot does come out empty past the quota, but the click
still lands, and a consumable chest despawns on the loot release - so a player
who is done deletes chests the players behind them still need. No data shape
fixes this: the client does not gate the interact cursor on the quest dynflag,
and stock's own quest chests (Olemba Cone 182541) behave the same way.

- GameObject::IsQuestChestUnavailableFor: chest that IsGameObjectForQuests, that
  ActivateToQuest rejects for this player, whose loot table holds nothing outside
  a quest gate, and which has no template-addon gold. Mixed treasure chests such
  as 153123 Kim'jael's Equipment are untouched.
- LootStore::HaveNonQuestLootFor -> LootTemplate::HasNonQuestDrop (+ LootGroup),
  recursive through references and groups.
- GameObject::BuildValuesUpdate ORs GO_FLAG_LOCKED | GO_FLAG_NOT_SELECTABLE into
  that one player's GAMEOBJECT_FLAGS, beside the existing chest.groupLootRules
  branch, GMs exempt. Quest chests force the field on EVERY update: the stored
  value never changes, so nothing dirties the mask, and if it only travelled
  while the lock applied then accepting the quest would leave the client holding
  a stale lock with the chest dead. Quest transitions run
  UpdateForQuestWorldObjects, so both edges land without a relog.
- Player::SendLoot refuses such a chest, so a client that ignores the flag cannot
  consume it either.

Closes I-284

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01R3mVmezJCwwVP8EYZdfYUq
